  <h2>5. Google Consent Mode v2 Architecture &amp; User Rights</h2>
  <p>
    We have engineered our frontend client to adhere strictly to <strong>Google Consent Mode v2</strong>, Google's advanced compliance standard designed for the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, and privacy-conscious jurisdictions worldwide.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you first arrive on our website, default consent parameters are automatically initialized to a restricted state across all four primary consent types:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ad_storage='denied'</code>: Disallows the storage of advertising-related cookies on your device.</li>
    <li><code>ad_user_data='denied'</code>: Disallows sending user data to Google for online advertising purposes.</li>
    <li><code>ad_personalization='denied'</code>: Disallows the use of collected data for personalized remarketing.</li>
    <li><code>analytics_storage='denied'</code>: Disallows storage of analytics tracking cookies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Only when an EEA or UK visitor affirmatively selects "Accept All" or activates advertising categories do these parameters dynamically transition to <code>'granted'</code>. If you select "Decline Non-Essential", our scripts immediately transmit anonymous pings to ensure ads are contextual only, without reading or writing persistent profiling identifiers to your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How to Manage, Block, or Delete Cookies via Browser Settings</h2>
  <p>
    In addition to using our website's consent controls, you retain total autonomy over your hardware and software. Every modern web browser provides comprehensive controls enabling you to inspect, block, or delete cookies and site data at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Follow these official, step-by-step instructions to configure cookie behavior within your specific web browser:
  </p>

  <h3>A. Google Chrome (Desktop &amp; Mobile)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Desktop (Windows / macOS / Linux):</strong> Click the three vertical dots menu in the top-right corner &gt; Select <em>Settings</em> &gt; Navigate to <em>Privacy and security</em> &gt; Click <em>Third-party cookies</em>. Here you can choose to "Block third-party cookies", "Allow third-party cookies", or specify individual site permissions. To purge existing cookies, choose <em>Clear browsing data</em>, check "Cookies and other site data", and select your desired timeframe.</li>
    <li><strong>Android:</strong> Open Chrome &gt; Tap the three-dot menu &gt; <em>Settings</em> &gt; <em>Site settings</em> &gt; <em>Cookies</em> &gt; Toggle third-party cookie restrictions or block entirely.</li>
    <li><strong>iOS (iPhone / iPad):</strong> Open iOS <em>Settings</em> &gt; Scroll to <em>Chrome</em> &gt; Toggle <em>Allow Cross-Website Tracking</em> off.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B. Apple Safari (macOS &amp; iOS)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> Open Safari &gt; Click <em>Safari</em> in the top menu bar &gt; Choose <em>Settings (Preferences)</em> &gt; Select the <em>Privacy</em> tab &gt; Ensure the checkbox <em>Prevent cross-site tracking</em> is enabled. To remove stored cookies, click <em>Manage Website Data...</em>, search for <code>ytubeconvert.site</code>, and click <em>Remove</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>iOS (iPhone / iPad):</strong> Open iOS <em>Settings</em> &gt; Tap <em>Safari</em> &gt; Under the <em>Privacy &amp; Security</em> section, turn on <em>Prevent Cross-Site Tracking</em> and optionally enable <em>Block All Cookies</em>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>C. Mozilla Firefox (Desktop &amp; Mobile)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Click the application menu (three horizontal lines) &gt; Select <em>Settings</em> &gt; Choose <em>Privacy &amp; Security</em> on the left panel &gt; Under <em>Enhanced Tracking Protection</em>, select <em>Standard</em> or <em>Strict</em> mode (which blocks cross-site tracking cookies, cryptominers, and social media trackers by default). To clear cookies, click <em>Clear Data...</em> under the Cookies and Site Data heading.</li>
    <li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Open Firefox &gt; Tap menu &gt; <em>Settings</em> &gt; <em>Enhanced Tracking Protection</em> &gt; Select <em>Strict</em>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>D. Microsoft Edge (Windows &amp; macOS)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Click the three dots in the top-right corner &gt; Choose <em>Settings</em> &gt; Navigate to <em>Cookies and site permissions</em> &gt; Click <em>Manage and delete cookies and site data</em> &gt; Toggle <em>Block third-party cookies</em> on. Under <em>Privacy, search, and services</em>, set Tracking Prevention to <em>Balanced</em> or <em>Strict</em>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Browser Privacy Signals: Do Not Track (DNT) &amp; Global Privacy Control (GPC)</h2>
  <p>
    Many advanced web browsers and privacy-oriented extensions support automated signals that communicate your privacy preferences directly to web servers upon every HTTP request:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC):</strong> GPC is an emerging browser specification legally recognized under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA) and various international privacy authorities. When our web application detects a valid GPC signal (<code>navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true</code>) transmitted by your browser, we automatically interpret this signal as a binding opt-out request for third-party targeted advertising cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Do Not Track (DNT):</strong> DNT is an older HTTP header (<code>DNT: 1</code>) indicating a user's request for third-party trackers to disable cross-site monitoring. While DNT lacks universal legal enforcement standards, our ad-loading architecture honors DNT headers by disabling ad personalization scripts whenever the signal is present.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Third-Party Web Advertising Networks &amp; Opt-Out Portals</h2>
  <p>
    If you wish to opt out of interest-based, behavioral targeted advertising across thousands of commercial advertising networks simultaneously, you may visit the industry-standard self-regulatory opt-out portals:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA) WebChoices Tool:</strong> <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://optout.aboutads.info/</a></li>
    <li><strong>Network Advertising Initiative (NAI) Consumer Opt-Out:</strong> <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://optout.networkadvertising.org/</a></li>
    <li><strong>European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance (EDAA - Your Online Choices):</strong> <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/</a></li>
    <li><strong>Google Ads Settings Portal:</strong> <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adssettings.google.com/</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. What Happens If You Disable All Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    We have engineered <strong>YouTube to MP4</strong> so that our core service remains fully functional even if you configure your web browser to completely block all HTTP cookies, third-party cookies, and storage items:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Conversion Functionality Unaffected:</strong> You can continue to paste YouTube URLs, inspect available video/audio streams, select resolutions (from 360p and 720p up to 1080p Full HD and 4K UHD), and download generated MP4 files with 100% operational fidelity. Our video conversion backend does not rely on persistent user cookies to process conversion jobs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visual Theme Reset:</strong> If <code>localStorage</code> is blocked, the website will not remember your Dark/Light theme selection between browser restarts, reverting to your operating system's default color scheme on each new page visit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Repeated Consent Prompts:</strong> Because the preference cookie recording your consent response cannot be stored, our cookie notification bar may reappear during subsequent browsing sessions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Updates &amp; Amendments to This Cookie Policy</h2>
  <p>
    As web standards evolve, new privacy regulations emerge, or we implement architectural modifications to our cloud infrastructure, we may update this Cookie Policy periodically. When changes occur, we will update the "Effective Date" and version reference at the beginning of this document. We encourage users to inspect this page periodically to remain informed about our ongoing data protection practices.
  </p>

